  "factor_name": "Regime-conditioned relative intermediate momentum",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "shift( cross_sectional_demean(pct_change(close,60)) * (2*I(cross_sectional_breadth_20d>=0.5)-1), 1)",
    "description": "Compute each asset's 60-day return relative to the contemporaneous cross-asset median. In broad positive regimes (at least half of assets have positive lagged 20-day returns), retain momentum; in weak-breadth regimes, invert the relative momentum signal to express defensive mean reversion. Shift the complete signal one session to prevent look-ahead."
